# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Kernl Next.js application.

## Implementation Details

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using npm
- Added as a production dependency in package.json
- Updated package-lock.json with resolved dependencies

### 2. Code Integration
- Updated `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx` to integrate Speed Insights
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag after the existing application structure
- Placed component at the end of body to ensure it loads after core application components

### 3. Framework-Specific Approach
- Followed the official Vercel documentation for Next.js 13.5+ applications
- Used the Next.js-specific import path: `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Integrated into the root layout to ensure Speed Insights tracking on all pages

### 4. Files Modified
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component

### 5. Verification Steps Completed
✓ Package installed successfully via npm
✓ Production build completed without errors
✓ ESLint passed with no warnings or errors
✓ TypeScript compilation successful
✓ All routes generated correctly (12 routes)

## Next Steps
To enable Speed Insights:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Vercel dashboard
3. Select the project
4. Go to Speed Insights in the sidebar
5. Click "Enable" to activate tracking

Once enabled and deployed, Speed Insights will automatically collect Web Vitals metrics from real user interactions and display them in the Vercel dashboard.

## Technical Notes
- The SpeedInsights component is a lightweight client-side tracker
- It automatically collects Core Web Vitals: LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB, INP
- The component only activates when deployed on Vercel with Speed Insights enabled
- No additional configuration is required for basic functionality
- The integration is non-blocking and won't affect application performance
